lit-frost: drop the gratuitous BLS/blst stack (prerequisite #2)
===============================================================
lit-frost's source uses no BLS, but it depends on lit-rust-crypto WITHOUT
default-features=false, so lit-rust-crypto's `default` feature (= blsful/default
+ blst) pulls in blsful -> blstrs_plus -> blst, a C library that will not
cross-compile to wasm32-unknown-unknown (cc-rs: "No available targets are
compatible with triple wasm32-unknown-unknown").

Fix: set default-features=false on the lit-rust-crypto dependency and drop the
explicit "blst" feature, keeping only the curve features lit-frost's code needs.
With this applied, the wrapper compiles to wasm32-unknown-unknown (cargo check,
0 errors). Upstream: make blst optional in lit-frost (don't enable it by default).

Against: lit-frost 0.4.0 (crates.io). Apply from the crate root:
    git apply lit-frost-no-blst.patch
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -115,8 +115,8 @@
 
 [dependencies.lit-rust-crypto]
 version = "0.6.0"
+default-features = false
 features = [
-    "blst",
     "curve25519-dalek-default",
     "decaf377-default",
     "elliptic-curve-default",
